#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "A free IBM course on quantum information and computation"
msgstr "Kursus IBM percuma tentang maklumat dan pengkomputeran kuantum"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: sidebar_label
#, no-wrap
msgid "Controlling error propagation"
msgstr "Mengawal perambatan ralat"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "{/* cspell:ignore transversally */}\n"
msgstr "{/* cspell:ignore transversally */}\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Fault-tolerant quantum computation is akin to a race between errors and error correction.\n"
"If the number of errors is small enough, error correction will successfully correct them; but if there are too many errors, error correction will fail.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pengkomputeran kuantum toleran ralat umpama perlumbaan antara ralat dan pembetulan ralat.\n"
"Jika bilangan ralat cukup kecil, pembetulan ralat akan berjaya membetulkannya; tetapi jika terlalu banyak ralat, pembetulan ralat akan gagal.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For this reason, sufficient care must be given to the way quantum computations are performed in fault-tolerant implementations of circuits, to control *error propagation.*\n"
"That is, an error on one qubit can potentially be propagated to multiple qubits through the action of gates in a quantum circuit, which can cause the number of errors to increase dramatically.\n"
"This is a paramount concern, for if we don't manage to control error propagation, our error-correction efforts will quickly be overwhelmed by errors.\n"
"If, on the other hand, we're able to keep the propagation of errors under control, then error correction stands a fighting chance of keeping up, allowing errors to be corrected at a high enough rate to allow the quantum computation to function as intended.\n"
msgstr ""
"Atas sebab ini, perhatian yang mencukupi mesti diberikan kepada cara pengiraan kuantum dilakukan dalam pelaksanaan litar yang toleran ralat, untuk mengawal *perambatan ralat.*\n"
"Iaitu, ralat pada satu qubit berpotensi merambat ke pelbagai qubit melalui tindakan get dalam litar kuantum, yang boleh menyebabkan bilangan ralat meningkat secara drastik.\n"
"Ini adalah kebimbangan utama, kerana jika kita gagal mengawal perambatan ralat, usaha pembetulan ralat kita akan cepat dilimpahi oleh ralat.\n"
"Sebaliknya, jika kita mampu mengawal perambatan ralat, maka pembetulan ralat berpeluang untuk berjalan seiring, membolehkan ralat dibetulkan pada kadar yang cukup tinggi agar pengiraan kuantum berfungsi seperti yang dimaksudkan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The starting point for a technical discussion of this issue is the recognition that two-qubit gates (or multiple-qubit gates more generally) can propagate errors, even when they function perfectly.\n"
"For instance, consider a controlled-NOT gate, and suppose that an $X$ error occurs on the control qubit just prior to the controlled-NOT gate being performed.\n"
"As we already observed in the \"Correcting quantum errors\" lesson, this is equivalent to an $X$ error occurring on *both* qubits after the controlled-NOT is performed. And the situation is similar for a $Z$ error acting on the target rather than the control prior to the controlled-NOT gate being performed.\n"
msgstr ""
"Titik permulaan untuk perbincangan teknikal isu ini ialah pengiktirafan bahawa get dua qubit (atau get berbilang qubit secara amnya) boleh merambatkan ralat, walaupun apabila ia berfungsi dengan sempurna.\n"
"Sebagai contoh, pertimbangkan get controlled-NOT, dan andaikan bahawa ralat $X$ berlaku pada qubit kawalan sebelum get controlled-NOT dilakukan.\n"
"Seperti yang telah kita perhatikan dalam pelajaran \"Membetulkan ralat kuantum\", ini bersamaan dengan ralat $X$ berlaku pada *kedua-dua* qubit selepas get controlled-NOT dilakukan. Dan situasinya serupa untuk ralat $Z$ yang bertindak pada sasaran berbanding kawalan sebelum get controlled-NOT dilakukan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Circuit representations of error propagation by CNOT "
"gates](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/fault-tolerant-quantum-computing/CNOT-error-propagation.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Circuit representations of error propagation by CNOT "
"gates](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/fault-tolerant-quantum-computing/CNOT-error-propagation.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is a *propagation of errors*, because the unfortunate location of an $X$ or $Z$ error prior to the controlled-NOT gate effectively turns it into two errors after the controlled-NOT gate.\n"
"This happens even when the controlled-NOT gate is perfect, and we must not forget that a given controlled-NOT gate may itself be noisy, which can *create* correlated errors on two qubits.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ini adalah *perambatan ralat*, kerana lokasi yang malang bagi ralat $X$ atau $Z$ sebelum get controlled-NOT secara efektifnya menjadikannya dua ralat selepas get controlled-NOT.\n"
"Ini berlaku walaupun get controlled-NOT adalah sempurna, dan kita tidak boleh lupa bahawa get controlled-NOT yang diberikan mungkin sendirinya mengandungi hingar, yang boleh *mewujudkan* ralat yang berkorelasi pada dua qubit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Adding to our concern is the fact that subsequent two-qubit gates might "
"propagate these errors even further, as the following figure suggests.\n"
msgstr ""
"Menambah kebimbangan kita ialah fakta bahawa get dua qubit berikutnya "
"mungkin merambatkan ralat ini lebih jauh lagi, seperti yang dicadangkan oleh"
" rajah berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Circuit representations of error propagation by multiple CNOT "
"gates](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/fault-tolerant-quantum-computing/multiple-CNOT-error-"
"propagation.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Circuit representations of error propagation by multiple CNOT "
"gates](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/fault-tolerant-quantum-computing/multiple-CNOT-error-"
"propagation.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In some sense, we can never get around this; so long as we use multiple-qubit gates, there will be a potential for error propagation.\n"
"However, as we'll discuss in the subsections that follow, steps can be taken to limit the damage this causes, allowing for propagated errors to be managed.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam erti kata tertentu, kita tidak pernah boleh mengelakkan ini; selagi kita menggunakan get berbilang qubit, akan selalu ada potensi untuk perambatan ralat.\n"
"Namun, seperti yang akan kita bincangkan dalam subseksyen berikut, langkah-langkah boleh diambil untuk mengehadkan kerosakan yang ditimbulkannya, membolehkan ralat yang merambat diuruskan.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Transversal gate implementations {#transversal-gate-implementations}"
msgstr "Pelaksanaan get transversal {#transversal-gate-implementations}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The simplest known way to mitigate error propagation in fault-tolerant quantum circuits is to implement gates *transversally*, which means building gadgets for them that have a certain simple form.\n"
"Specifically, the gadgets must be a *tensor product* of operations (or, in other words, a depth-one quantum circuit), where each operation can only act on a single qubit *position* within each code block that it touches.\n"
"This is perhaps easiest to explain through some examples.\n"
msgstr ""
"Cara paling mudah yang diketahui untuk mengurangkan perambatan ralat dalam litar kuantum toleran ralat ialah melaksanakan get secara *transversal*, yang bermaksud membina gadget untuknya yang mempunyai bentuk mudah tertentu.\n"
"Khususnya, gadget mestilah berupa *hasil darab tensor* operasi (atau, dalam erti kata lain, litar kuantum kedalaman satu), di mana setiap operasi hanya boleh bertindak pada satu *kedudukan* qubit tunggal dalam setiap blok kod yang disentuhnya.\n"
"Ini mungkin paling mudah dijelaskan melalui beberapa contoh.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Examples of transversal gate implementations {#examples-of-transversal-gate-"
"implementations}"
msgstr ""
"Contoh pelaksanaan get transversal {#examples-of-transversal-gate-"
"implementations}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Consider the following figure, which suggests a transversal implementation "
"of a CNOT gate. (This particular implementation, where CNOTs are performed "
"qubit by qubit, only works for CSS codes — but it does, in fact, work for "
"*all* CSS codes.)\n"
msgstr ""
"Pertimbangkan rajah berikut, yang menunjukkan pelaksanaan transversal get "
"CNOT. (Pelaksanaan tertentu ini, di mana CNOT dilakukan qubit demi qubit, "
"hanya berfungsi untuk kod CSS — tetapi ia memang berfungsi untuk *semua* kod"
" CSS.)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Transversal implementation of a CNOT "
"gate](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/fault-tolerant-quantum-computing/transversal-CNOT.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Transversal implementation of a CNOT "
"gate](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/fault-tolerant-quantum-computing/transversal-CNOT.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"There are two code blocks in this figure, each depicted as consisting of five qubits (although it could be more, as has already been suggested).\n"
"The circuit on the right has depth one, and each of the CNOT gates acts on a single qubit position within each block:\n"
"both the control and target for the first CNOT is the topmost qubit (that is, qubit 0 using the Qiskit numbering convention),\n"
"both the control and target for the second CNOT is the qubit second from top (that is, qubit 1), and so on.\n"
"Hence, this is a transversal gadget.\n"
msgstr ""
"Terdapat dua blok kod dalam rajah ini, masing-masing digambarkan terdiri daripada lima qubit (walaupun boleh lebih, seperti yang telah dicadangkan).\n"
"Litar di sebelah kanan mempunyai kedalaman satu, dan setiap get CNOT bertindak pada satu kedudukan qubit dalam setiap blok:\n"
"kawalan dan sasaran untuk CNOT pertama adalah qubit paling atas (iaitu, qubit 0 menggunakan konvensyen penomboran Qiskit),\n"
"kawalan dan sasaran untuk CNOT kedua adalah qubit kedua dari atas (iaitu, qubit 1), dan seterusnya.\n"
"Oleh itu, ini adalah gadget transversal.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For a second example — really a class of examples — consider any Pauli gate.\n"
"Pauli gates can always be implemented transversally, for any stabilizer code, by building gadgets that are composed of Pauli operations.\n"
"In particular, every Pauli operation on a logical qubit encoded by a stabilizer code can be implemented transversally by choosing an appropriate Pauli operation on the physical qubits used for the encoding.\n"
"This is consistent with a fact that was mentioned in passing in the \"Stabilizer formalism\" lesson: up to a global phase, Pauli operations that commute with every stabilizer generator of a stabilizer code act like Pauli operations on the qubit or qubits encoded by that code.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk contoh kedua — sebenarnya kelas contoh — pertimbangkan mana-mana get Pauli.\n"
"get Pauli sentiasa boleh dilaksanakan secara transversal, untuk mana-mana kod penstabil, dengan membina gadget yang terdiri daripada operasi Pauli.\n"
"Khususnya, setiap operasi Pauli pada qubit logik yang dikodkan oleh kod penstabil boleh dilaksanakan secara transversal dengan memilih operasi Pauli yang sesuai pada qubit fizikal yang digunakan untuk pengekodan.\n"
"Ini konsisten dengan fakta yang disebutkan secara sambil lewa dalam pelajaran \"Formalisme penstabil\": sehingga fasa global, operasi Pauli yang bertukar dengan setiap penjana penstabil kod penstabil bertindak seperti operasi Pauli pada qubit atau qubit yang dikodkan oleh kod tersebut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As a specific example, consider the $9$-qubit Shor code, for which standard "
"basis states could be encoded as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sebagai contoh khusus, pertimbangkan kod Shor $9$-qubit, di mana keadaan "
"asas piawai boleh dikodkan seperti berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\vert 0\\rangle &\n"
"\\:\\mapsto\\:\n"
"\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"(\\vert 000\\rangle + \\vert 111\\rangle) \\otimes\n"
"(\\vert 000\\rangle + \\vert 111\\rangle) \\otimes\n"
"(\\vert 000\\rangle + \\vert 111\\rangle) \\\\[3mm]\n"
"\\vert 1\\rangle &\n"
"\\:\\mapsto\\:\n"
"\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"(\\vert 000\\rangle - \\vert 111\\rangle) \\otimes\n"
"(\\vert 000\\rangle - \\vert 111\\rangle) \\otimes\n"
"(\\vert 000\\rangle - \\vert 111\\rangle)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\vert 0\\rangle &\n"
"\\:\\mapsto\\:\n"
"\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"(\\vert 000\\rangle + \\vert 111\\rangle) \\otimes\n"
"(\\vert 000\\rangle + \\vert 111\\rangle) \\otimes\n"
"(\\vert 000\\rangle + \\vert 111\\rangle) \\\\[3mm]\n"
"\\vert 1\\rangle &\n"
"\\:\\mapsto\\:\n"
"\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"(\\vert 000\\rangle - \\vert 111\\rangle) \\otimes\n"
"(\\vert 000\\rangle - \\vert 111\\rangle) \\otimes\n"
"(\\vert 000\\rangle - \\vert 111\\rangle)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"An $X$ gate on the logical qubit encoded by this code can be implemented "
"transversally by the $9$-qubit Pauli operation\n"
msgstr ""
"get $X$ pada qubit logik yang dikodkan oleh kod ini boleh dilaksanakan "
"secara transversal oleh operasi Pauli $9$-qubit\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"Z \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes\n"
"Z \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes\n"
"Z \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"Z \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes\n"
"Z \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes\n"
"Z \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"while a $Z$ gate on the logical qubit can be implemented transversally by "
"the $9$-qubit Pauli operation\n"
msgstr ""
"manakala get $Z$ pada qubit logik boleh dilaksanakan secara transversal oleh"
" operasi Pauli $9$-qubit\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"X \\otimes X \\otimes X \\otimes\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"X \\otimes X \\otimes X \\otimes\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Both of these Pauli operations have weight $3,$ which is the minimum weight required.\n"
"(The $9$-qubit Shor code has distance $3,$ so any non-identity Pauli operation of weight $2$ or less is detected as an error.)\n"
msgstr ""
"Kedua-dua operasi Pauli ini mempunyai berat $3,$ iaitu berat minimum yang diperlukan.\n"
"(Kod Shor $9$-qubit mempunyai jarak $3,$ jadi mana-mana operasi Pauli bukan identiti dengan berat $2$ atau kurang dikesan sebagai ralat.)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"And, for a third example, the $7$-qubit Steane code (and indeed every color code) allows for a transversal implementation of *all* Clifford gates.\n"
"We've already seen how CNOT gates are implemented transversally for any CSS code, so it remains to consider $H$ and $S$ gates.\n"
"A Hadamard gate applied to all $7$ qubits of the Steane code is equivalent to $H$ being applied to the logical qubit it encodes, while an $S^{\\dagger}$ gate (as opposed to an $S$ gate) applied to all $7$ qubits is equivalent to a logical $S$ gate.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dan, untuk contoh ketiga, kod Steane $7$-qubit (dan memang setiap kod warna) membenarkan pelaksanaan transversal bagi *semua* get Clifford.\n"
"Kita sudah melihat bagaimana get CNOT dilaksanakan secara transversal untuk mana-mana kod CSS, jadi tinggal lagi untuk mempertimbangkan get $H$ dan $S$.\n"
"get Hadamard yang digunakan pada semua $7$ qubit kod Steane bersamaan dengan $H$ yang digunakan pada qubit logik yang dikodkannya, manakala get $S^{\\dagger}$ (berbanding get $S$) yang digunakan pada semua $7$ qubit bersamaan dengan get $S$ logik.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Error propagation for transversal gadgets {#error-propagation-for-"
"transversal-gadgets}"
msgstr ""
"Perambatan ralat untuk gadget transversal {#error-propagation-for-"
"transversal-gadgets}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now that we know what transversal implementations of gates are, let us "
"discuss their connection to error propagation.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kini kita tahu apa itu pelaksanaan transversal get, mari kita bincangkan "
"hubungannya dengan perambatan ralat.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For a transversal implementation of a single-qubit gate, we simply have a tensor product of single-qubit gates in our gadget, which acts on a code block of physical qubits for the chosen quantum error correcting code.\n"
"Although any of these gates could fail and introduce an error, there will be no *propagation* of errors because no multiple-qubit gates are involved.\n"
"Immediately after the gadget is applied, error correction is performed; and if the number of errors introduced by the gadget (or while the gadget is being performed) is sufficiently small, the errors will be corrected.\n"
"So, if the rate of errors introduced by faulty gates is sufficiently small, error correction has a good chance to succeed.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk pelaksanaan transversal get satu qubit, kita hanya mempunyai hasil darab tensor get satu qubit dalam gadget kita, yang bertindak pada blok kod qubit fizikal untuk kod pembetulan ralat kuantum yang dipilih.\n"
"Walaupun mana-mana get ini boleh gagal dan memperkenalkan ralat, tidak akan ada *perambatan* ralat kerana tiada get berbilang qubit yang terlibat.\n"
"Sejurus selepas gadget digunakan, pembetulan ralat dilakukan; dan jika bilangan ralat yang diperkenalkan oleh gadget (atau semasa gadget sedang dilakukan) cukup kecil, ralat akan dibetulkan.\n"
"Jadi, jika kadar ralat yang diperkenalkan oleh get yang rosak cukup kecil, pembetulan ralat berpeluang baik untuk berjaya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For a transversal implementation of a two-qubit gate, on the other hand, there is the potential for a propagation of errors — there is simply no way to avoid this, as we have already observed.\n"
"The essential point, however, is that a transversal gadget can never cause a propagation of errors\n"
"*within a single code block*.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk pelaksanaan transversal get dua qubit pula, terdapat potensi untuk perambatan ralat — memang tidak ada cara untuk mengelakkan ini, seperti yang telah kita perhatikan.\n"
"Perkara penting, bagaimanapun, ialah gadget transversal tidak pernah boleh menyebabkan perambatan ralat\n"
"*dalam satu blok kod tunggal*.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For example, considering the transversal implementation of a CNOT gate for a CSS code described above, an $X$ error could occur on the top qubit of the top code block right before the gadget is performed, and the first CNOT within the gadget will propagate that error to the top qubit in the lower block.\n"
"However, the two resulting errors are now in *separate* code blocks.\n"
"So, assuming our code can correct an $X$ error, the error correction steps that take place after the gadget will correct the two $X$ errors individually — because only a single error occurs within each code block.\n"
"In contrast, if error propagation were to happen inside of the *same* code block, it could turn a low-weight error into a high-weight error that the code cannot handle.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sebagai contoh, mempertimbangkan pelaksanaan transversal get CNOT untuk kod CSS yang diterangkan di atas, ralat $X$ boleh berlaku pada qubit paling atas blok kod atas sejurus sebelum gadget dilakukan, dan CNOT pertama dalam gadget akan merambatkan ralat tersebut ke qubit paling atas dalam blok bawah.\n"
"Namun, dua ralat yang terhasil kini berada dalam *blok kod yang berasingan*.\n"
"Jadi, dengan mengandaikan kod kita boleh membetulkan ralat $X$, langkah pembetulan ralat yang berlaku selepas gadget akan membetulkan dua ralat $X$ secara berasingan — kerana hanya satu ralat berlaku dalam setiap blok kod.\n"
"Sebaliknya, jika perambatan ralat berlaku di dalam blok kod yang *sama*, ia boleh mengubah ralat berat rendah menjadi ralat berat tinggi yang tidak dapat dikendalikan oleh kod.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Non-universality of transversal gates {#non-universality-of-transversal-"
"gates}"
msgstr ""
"Bukan-keuniversalan get transversal {#non-universality-of-transversal-gates}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For two different stabilizer codes, it may be that a particular gate can be implemented transversally with one code but not the other.\n"
"For example, while it is not possible to implement a $T$ gate transversally using the $7$-qubit Steane code, there are other codes for which this is possible.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk dua kod penstabil yang berbeza, mungkin saja get tertentu boleh dilaksanakan secara transversal dengan satu kod tetapi tidak dengan yang lain.\n"
"Sebagai contoh, walaupun tidak mungkin melaksanakan get $T$ secara transversal menggunakan kod Steane $7$-qubit, terdapat kod lain yang memungkinkan ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Unfortunately, it is never possible, for any non-trivial quantum error correcting code, to implement a *universal* set of gates transversally.\n"
"This fact is known as the *Eastin-Knill theorem*.\n"
msgstr ""
"Malangnya, tidak pernah mungkin, untuk mana-mana kod pembetulan ralat kuantum yang tidak trivial, melaksanakan set get *universal* secara transversal.\n"
"Fakta ini dikenali sebagai *teorem Eastin-Knill*.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Figure title=\"Theorem\">\n"
"Eastin-Knill theorem: For any quantum error correcting code with distance at least 2, the set of logical gates that can be implemented transversally generates a set of operations that (up to a global phase) is discrete, and is therefore not universal.\n"
"</Figure>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Figure title=\"Teorem\">\n"
"Teorem Eastin-Knill: Untuk mana-mana kod pembetulan ralat kuantum dengan jarak sekurang-kurangnya 2, set get logik yang boleh dilaksanakan secara transversal menjana set operasi yang (sehingga fasa global) adalah diskrit, dan oleh itu tidak universal.\n"
"</Figure>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The proof of this theorem will not be explained here.\n"
"(It is not a complicated proof, but it does require a basic knowledge of Lie groups and Lie algebras, which are not among the series prerequisites.)\n"
"The basic idea, however, can be conveyed in intuitive terms:\n"
"Infinite families of transversal operations can't possibly stay within the code space of a non-trivial code because minuscule differences in transversal operations are well-approximated by low-weight Pauli operations, which the code detects as errors.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bukti teorem ini tidak akan dijelaskan di sini.\n"
"(Ia bukan bukti yang rumit, tetapi memerlukan pengetahuan asas tentang kumpulan Lie dan aljabar Lie, yang bukan antara prasyarat siri ini.)\n"
"Namun, idea asasnya boleh disampaikan dalam istilah intuitif:\n"
"Keluarga tak terhingga operasi transversal tidak mungkin kekal dalam ruang kod bagi kod tidak trivial kerana perbezaan halus dalam operasi transversal dihampiri dengan baik oleh operasi Pauli berat rendah, yang dikesan oleh kod sebagai ralat.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In summary, transversal gadgets offer a simple and inherently fault-tolerant"
" implementation of gates — but for any reasonable choice of a quantum error "
"correcting code, there will never be a universal gate set that can be "
"implemented in this way, which necessitates the use of alternative "
"gadgets.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ringkasnya, gadget transversal menawarkan pelaksanaan get yang mudah dan "
"secara inheren toleran ralat — tetapi untuk mana-mana pilihan kod pembetulan"
" ralat kuantum yang munasabah, tidak akan pernah ada set get universal yang "
"boleh dilaksanakan dengan cara ini, yang memerlukan penggunaan gadget "
"alternatif.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Magic states {#magic-states}"
msgstr "Keadaan ajaib {#magic-states}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Given that it is not possible, for any non-trivial choice for a quantum error correcting code, to implement a universal set of quantum gates transversally, we must consider other methods to implement gates fault-tolerantly.\n"
"One well-known method is based on the notion of *magic states*, which are quantum states of qubits that enable fault-tolerant implementations of certain gates.\n"
msgstr ""
"Memandangkan tidak mungkin, untuk mana-mana pilihan kod pembetulan ralat kuantum yang tidak trivial, melaksanakan set get kuantum universal secara transversal, kita perlu mempertimbangkan kaedah lain untuk melaksanakan get secara toleran ralat.\n"
"Satu kaedah yang terkenal berdasarkan gagasan *keadaan ajaib*, iaitu keadaan kuantum qubit yang membolehkan pelaksanaan toleran ralat bagi get tertentu.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Implementing gates with magic states {#implementing-gates-with-magic-states}"
msgstr ""
"Melaksanakan get dengan keadaan ajaib {#implementing-gates-with-magic-"
"states}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Let us begin by considering $S$ and $T$ gates, which have matrix "
"descriptions as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Mari mulakan dengan mempertimbangkan get $S$ dan $T$, yang mempunyai "
"penerangan matriks seperti berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"S = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0\\\\\n"
"0 & i\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0\\\\\n"
"0 & e^{i\\pi/2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\qquad\\text{and}\\qquad\n"
"T = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0\\\\\n"
"0 & \\frac{1+i}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0\\\\\n"
"0 & e^{i\\pi/4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"S = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0\\\\\n"
"0 & i\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0\\\\\n"
"0 & e^{i\\pi/2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\qquad\\text{and}\\qquad\n"
"T = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0\\\\\n"
"0 & \\frac{1+i}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0\\\\\n"
"0 & e^{i\\pi/4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"By definition, $S$ is a Clifford operation, while $T$ is not;\n"
"it is not possible to implement a $T$ gate with a circuit composed of Clifford gates ($H$ gates, $S$ gates, and CNOT gates).\n"
msgstr ""
"Mengikut definisi, $S$ adalah operasi Clifford, manakala $T$ tidak;\n"
"tidak mungkin melaksanakan get $T$ dengan litar yang terdiri daripada get Clifford (get $H$, get $S$, dan get CNOT).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"However, it is possible to implement a $T$ gate (up to a global phase) with "
"a circuit composed of Clifford gates if, in addition, we have a copy of the "
"state\n"
msgstr ""
"Namun, adalah mungkin untuk melaksanakan get $T$ (sehingga fasa global) "
"dengan litar yang terdiri daripada get Clifford jika, selain itu, kita "
"mempunyai salinan keadaan\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"T\\vert {+} \\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0 \\rangle + \\frac{e^{i\\pi/4}}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 1\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"T\\vert {+} \\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0 \\rangle + \\frac{e^{i\\pi/4}}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 1\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"and we allow for standard basis measurements and for gates to be classically controlled.\n"
"In particular, the following circuit shows one way to do this.\n"
"The phenomenon on display here is a somewhat simplified example of *quantum gate teleportation*.\n"
msgstr ""
"dan kita membenarkan pengukuran asas piawai dan get yang dikawal secara klasik.\n"
"Khususnya, litar berikut menunjukkan satu cara untuk melakukan ini.\n"
"Fenomena yang dipaparkan di sini adalah contoh yang agak dipermudahkan bagi *teleportasi get kuantum*.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![A circuit diagram depicting magic state "
"injection](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/fault-tolerant-quantum-computing/magic-state-injection.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![A circuit diagram depicting magic state "
"injection](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/fault-tolerant-quantum-computing/magic-state-injection.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To check that this circuit works correctly, we can first compute the action "
"of the CNOT gate on the input.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk memeriksa bahawa litar ini berfungsi dengan betul, kita boleh terlebih"
" dahulu mengira tindakan get CNOT pada input.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"T \\vert {+} \\rangle \\otimes \\vert\\psi\\rangle\n"
"\\stackrel{\\text{CNOT}}{\\longmapsto}\n"
"\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0\\rangle \\otimes T \\vert \\psi\\rangle + \\frac{1+i}{2} \\vert 1\\rangle \\otimes T^{\\dagger} \\vert \\psi\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"T \\vert {+} \\rangle \\otimes \\vert\\psi\\rangle\n"
"\\stackrel{\\text{CNOT}}{\\longmapsto}\n"
"\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0\\rangle \\otimes T \\vert \\psi\\rangle + \\frac{1+i}{2} \\vert 1\\rangle \\otimes T^{\\dagger} \\vert \\psi\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The measurement therefore gives the outcomes $0$ and $1$ with equal probability.\n"
"If the outcome is $0,$ the $S$ gate is not performed, and the output state is $T\\vert\\psi\\rangle;$ and\n"
"if the outcome is $1,$ the $S$ gate is performed, and the output state is $ST^{\\dagger}\\vert\\psi\\rangle = T\\vert \\psi\\rangle.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Pengukuran oleh itu memberikan hasil $0$ dan $1$ dengan kebarangkalian yang sama.\n"
"Jika hasilnya $0,$ get $S$ tidak dilakukan, dan keadaan output adalah $T\\vert\\psi\\rangle;$ dan\n"
"jika hasilnya $1,$ get $S$ dilakukan, dan keadaan output adalah $ST^{\\dagger}\\vert\\psi\\rangle = T\\vert \\psi\\rangle.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The state $T\\vert {+}\\rangle$ is called a *magic state* in this context, although it's not unique in this regard: other states are also called magic states when they can be used in a similar way (for possibly different gates and using different circuits).\n"
"For example, exchanging the state $T\\vert{+}\\rangle$ for the state $S\\vert{+}\\rangle$ and replacing the $S$ gate in the circuit above with a $Z$ gate implements an $S$ gate — which is potentially useful for fault-tolerant quantum computation using a code for which $S$ gates cannot be implemented transversally.\n"
msgstr ""
"Keadaan $T\\vert {+}\\rangle$ dipanggil *keadaan ajaib* dalam konteks ini, walaupun ia tidak unik dalam hal ini: keadaan lain juga dipanggil keadaan ajaib apabila ia boleh digunakan dengan cara yang serupa (untuk get yang mungkin berbeza dan menggunakan litar yang berbeza).\n"
"Sebagai contoh, menggantikan keadaan $T\\vert{+}\\rangle$ dengan keadaan $S\\vert{+}\\rangle$ dan menggantikan get $S$ dalam litar di atas dengan get $Z$ melaksanakan get $S$ — yang berpotensi berguna untuk pengkomputeran kuantum toleran ralat menggunakan kod yang tidak dapat melaksanakan get $S$ secara transversal.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Fault-tolerant gadgets from magic states {#fault-tolerant-gadgets-from-"
"magic-states}"
msgstr ""
"Gadget toleran ralat daripada keadaan ajaib {#fault-tolerant-gadgets-from-"
"magic-states}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It may not be clear that using magic states to implement gates is helpful for fault-tolerance.\n"
"For the $T$ gate implementation described above, for instance, it appears that we still need to apply a $T$ gate to a $\\vert{+}\\rangle$ state to obtain a magic state, which we then use to implement a $T$ gate.\n"
"So what is the advantage of using this approach for fault-tolerance?\n"
msgstr ""
"Mungkin tidak jelas bahawa menggunakan keadaan ajaib untuk melaksanakan get berguna untuk toleransi ralat.\n"
"Untuk pelaksanaan get $T$ yang diterangkan di atas, sebagai contoh, nampaknya kita masih perlu menggunakan get $T$ pada keadaan $\\vert{+}\\rangle$ untuk mendapatkan keadaan ajaib, yang kemudian kita gunakan untuk melaksanakan get $T$.\n"
"Jadi apakah kelebihan menggunakan pendekatan ini untuk toleransi ralat?\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Here are three key points that provide an answer to this question.\n"
msgstr ""
"Berikut adalah tiga perkara penting yang memberikan jawapan kepada soalan "
"ini.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The creation of magic states does not necessitate applying the gate we're "
"attempting to implement to a particular state. For example, applying a $T$ "
"gate to a $\\vert {+} \\rangle$ state is not the only way to obtain a "
"$T\\vert{+}\\rangle$ state.\n"
msgstr ""
"Penciptaan keadaan ajaib tidak memerlukan penggunaan get yang cuba kita "
"laksanakan pada keadaan tertentu. Sebagai contoh, menggunakan get $T$ pada "
"keadaan $\\vert {+} \\rangle$ bukan satu-satunya cara untuk mendapatkan "
"keadaan $T\\vert{+}\\rangle$.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The creation of magic states can be done separately from the computation in "
"which they're used. This means that errors that arise in the magic state "
"creation process will not propagate to the actual computation being "
"performed.\n"
msgstr ""
"Penciptaan keadaan ajaib boleh dilakukan secara berasingan daripada "
"pengiraan di mana ia digunakan. Ini bermakna ralat yang timbul dalam proses "
"penciptaan keadaan ajaib tidak akan merambat ke pengiraan sebenar yang "
"sedang dilakukan.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If the individual gates in the circuit implementing a chosen gate using a "
"magic state can be implemented fault-tolerantly, and we assume the "
"availability of magic states, we obtain a fault-tolerant implementation of "
"the chosen gate.\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika get individu dalam litar yang melaksanakan get yang dipilih menggunakan"
" keadaan ajaib boleh dilaksanakan secara toleran ralat, dan kita "
"mengandaikan ketersediaan keadaan ajaib, kita mendapatkan pelaksanaan "
"toleran ralat bagi get yang dipilih.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To simplify the discussion that follows, let's focus in on $T$ gates specifically — keeping in mind that the methodology can be extended to other gates.\n"
"A fault-tolerant implementation of a $T$ gate using magic states takes the form suggested by the following figure.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk memudahkan perbincangan yang berikut, mari kita fokus pada get $T$ khusus — dengan mengingat bahawa metodologi boleh dilanjutkan ke get lain.\n"
"Pelaksanaan toleran ralat get $T$ menggunakan keadaan ajaib mengambil bentuk yang dicadangkan oleh rajah berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![A circuit diagram depicting magic state injection on an encoded "
"qubit](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/fault-tolerant-quantum-computing/encoded-magic-state-"
"injection.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![A circuit diagram depicting magic state injection on an encoded "
"qubit](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/fault-tolerant-quantum-computing/encoded-magic-state-"
"injection.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Qubits in the original $T$-gate circuit correspond to logical qubits in this diagram, which are encoded by whatever code we're using for fault-tolerance.\n"
"The inputs and outputs in the diagram should therefore be understood as *encodings* of these states.\n"
"This means, in particular, that we actually don't need just magic states — we need *encoded* magic states.\n"
"The gates in the original $T$-gate circuit are here replaced by gadgets, which we assume are fault-tolerant.\n"
msgstr ""
"qubit dalam litar get $T$ asal sepadan dengan qubit logik dalam gambar rajah ini, yang dikodkan oleh kod yang kita gunakan untuk toleransi ralat.\n"
"Input dan output dalam gambar rajah oleh itu perlu difahami sebagai *pengekodan* keadaan-keadaan ini.\n"
"Ini bermakna, khususnya, kita sebenarnya tidak hanya memerlukan keadaan ajaib — kita memerlukan keadaan ajaib yang *dikodkan*.\n"
"get dalam litar get $T$ asal di sini digantikan oleh gadget, yang kita andaikan adalah toleran ralat.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This particular figure therefore suggests that we already have fault-tolerant gadgets for CNOT gates and $S$ gates.\n"
"For a color code, these gadgets could be transversal;\n"
"for a surface code (or any other CSS code), the CNOT can be performed transversally, while the $S$ gate gadget might itself be implemented using magic states, as was earlier suggested is possible.\n"
"(The figure also suggests that we have a fault-tolerant gadget for performing a standard basis measurement, which we've ignored thus far.\n"
"This could actually be challenging for some codes selected to make it so, but for a CSS code it's a matter of measuring each physical qubit followed by classical post-processing.)\n"
msgstr ""
"Rajah tertentu ini oleh itu menunjukkan bahawa kita sudah mempunyai gadget toleran ralat untuk get CNOT dan get $S$.\n"
"Untuk kod warna, gadget ini boleh bersifat transversal;\n"
"untuk kod permukaan (atau mana-mana kod CSS lain), CNOT boleh dilakukan secara transversal, manakala gadget get $S$ mungkin sendirinya dilaksanakan menggunakan keadaan ajaib, seperti yang dicadangkan sebelum ini adalah mungkin.\n"
"(Rajah ini juga menunjukkan bahawa kita mempunyai gadget toleran ralat untuk melakukan pengukuran asas piawai, yang telah kita abaikan setakat ini.\n"
"Ini sebenarnya boleh menjadi cabaran untuk beberapa kod yang dipilih untuk membuatnya demikian, tetapi untuk kod CSS ia adalah soal mengukur setiap qubit fizikal diikuti dengan pemprosesan pasca secara klasik.)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The implementation is therefore fault-tolerant, assuming we have an encoding of a magic state $T\\vert{+}\\rangle.$\n"
"But, we still haven't addressed the issue of how we obtain an encoding of this state.\n"
"One way to obtain encoded magic states (or, perhaps more accurately, to make them better) is through a process known as *magic state distillation.*\n"
"The following diagram illustrates what this process looks like at the highest level.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pelaksanaan ini oleh itu toleran ralat, dengan mengandaikan kita mempunyai pengekodan keadaan ajaib $T\\vert{+}\\rangle.$\n"
"Tetapi, kita masih belum menangani isu bagaimana kita mendapatkan pengekodan keadaan ini.\n"
"Satu cara untuk mendapatkan keadaan ajaib yang dikodkan (atau, mungkin lebih tepat, untuk menjadikannya lebih baik) adalah melalui proses yang dikenali sebagai *penyulingan keadaan ajaib.*\n"
"Gambar rajah berikut menggambarkan bagaimana proses ini kelihatan pada peringkat tertinggi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![A circuit diagram representing distillation of encoded magic "
"states](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/fault-tolerant-quantum-computing/encoded-magic-state-"
"distillation.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![A circuit diagram representing distillation of encoded magic "
"states](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/fault-tolerant-quantum-computing/encoded-magic-state-"
"distillation.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In words, a collection of noisy encoded magic states is fed into a special type of circuit known as a *distiller*.\n"
"All but one of the output blocks is measured — meaning that *logical* qubits are measured with standard basis measurements.\n"
"If any of the measurement outcomes is $1,$ the process has failed and must be restarted.\n"
"If, however, every measurement outcome is $0,$ the resulting state of the top code block will be a less noisy encoded magic state.\n"
"This state could then join four more as inputs into another distiller, or used to implement a $T$ gate if it is deemed to be sufficiently close to a true encoded magic state.\n"
"Of course, the process must begin somewhere, with one possibility being to prepare them non-fault-tolerantly.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam kata-kata, sekumpulan keadaan ajaib yang dikodkan dengan hingar dimasukkan ke dalam jenis litar khas yang dikenali sebagai *penyuling*.\n"
"Semua blok output kecuali satu diukur — bermaksud qubit *logik* diukur dengan pengukuran asas piawai.\n"
"Jika mana-mana hasil pengukuran adalah $1,$ proses gagal dan mesti dimulakan semula.\n"
"Namun, jika setiap hasil pengukuran adalah $0,$ keadaan yang terhasil bagi blok kod atas akan menjadi keadaan ajaib yang dikodkan dengan hingar yang lebih sedikit.\n"
"Keadaan ini kemudian boleh bergabung dengan empat lagi sebagai input ke dalam penyuling lain, atau digunakan untuk melaksanakan get $T$ jika ia dianggap cukup dekat dengan keadaan ajaib yang dikodkan sebenar.\n"
"Sudah tentu, proses mesti bermula dari suatu tempat, dengan satu kemungkinan ialah menyediakannya secara tidak toleran ralat.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"There are different known ways to build the distiller itself, but they will not be explained or analyzed here.\n"
"At a logical level, the typical approach — remarkably and somewhat coincidentally — is to run an encoding circuit for a stabilizer code in reverse!\n"
"This could, in fact, be a different stabilizer code from the one used for error correction.\n"
"For example, one could potentially use a surface or color code for error correction, but run an encoder for the $5$-qubit code in reverse for the sake of magic state distillation.\n"
"Encoding circuits for stabilizer codes only require Clifford gates, which simplifies the fault-tolerant implementation of a distiller.\n"
"In actuality, the specifics are dependent on the codes that are used.\n"
msgstr ""
"Terdapat cara berbeza yang diketahui untuk membina penyuling itu sendiri, tetapi tidak akan dijelaskan atau dianalisis di sini.\n"
"Pada peringkat logik, pendekatan tipikal — secara luar biasa dan agak kebetulan — adalah menjalankan litar pengekodan untuk kod penstabil secara terbalik!\n"
"Ini sebenarnya boleh menjadi kod penstabil yang berbeza daripada yang digunakan untuk pembetulan ralat.\n"
"Sebagai contoh, seseorang boleh berpotensi menggunakan kod permukaan atau warna untuk pembetulan ralat, tetapi menjalankan pengekod untuk kod $5$-qubit secara terbalik bagi tujuan penyulingan keadaan ajaib.\n"
"Litar pengekodan untuk kod penstabil hanya memerlukan get Clifford, yang memudahkan pelaksanaan toleran ralat penyuling.\n"
"Sebenarnya, spesifik bergantung pada kod yang digunakan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In summary, this section has aimed to provide only a very high-level discussion of magic states, with the intention being to provide just a basic idea of how it works.\n"
"It is sometimes claimed that the overhead for using magic states to implement gates fault-tolerantly along these lines would be extremely high, with the vast majority of the work going into the distillation process.\n"
"However, this is actually not so clear — there are many potential ways to optimize these processes.\n"
"There are, in addition, alternative approaches to building fault-tolerant gadgets for gates that cannot be implemented transversally.\n"
"For example, *code deformation* and *code switching* are keywords associated with some of these schemes — and new ways continue to be developed and refined.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ringkasnya, bahagian ini bertujuan untuk memberikan perbincangan peringkat tinggi yang sangat asas tentang keadaan ajaib, dengan niat hanya memberikan idea asas tentang cara ia berfungsi.\n"
"Kadangkala dituntut bahawa overhead untuk menggunakan keadaan ajaib bagi melaksanakan get secara toleran ralat mengikut garis ini akan sangat tinggi, dengan sebahagian besar kerja pergi ke dalam proses penyulingan.\n"
"Namun, ini sebenarnya tidak begitu jelas — terdapat banyak cara berpotensi untuk mengoptimumkan proses-proses ini.\n"
"Selain itu, terdapat pendekatan alternatif untuk membina gadget toleran ralat bagi get yang tidak boleh dilaksanakan secara transversal.\n"
"Sebagai contoh, *perubahan bentuk kod* dan *penukaran kod* adalah kata kunci yang berkaitan dengan beberapa skim ini — dan cara-cara baru terus dibangunkan dan diperhalusi.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Fault-tolerant error correction {#fault-tolerant-error-correction}"
msgstr "Pembetulan ralat toleran ralat {#fault-tolerant-error-correction}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In addition to the implementation of the various gadgets required for a fault-tolerant implementation of a given quantum circuit, there is another important issue that must be recognized: the implementation of the error correction steps themselves.\n"
"This goes back to the idea that anything involving quantum information is susceptible to errors — including the circuits that are themselves meant to correct errors.\n"
msgstr ""
"Selain daripada pelaksanaan pelbagai gadget yang diperlukan untuk pelaksanaan toleran ralat bagi litar kuantum yang diberikan, terdapat isu penting lain yang perlu diakui: pelaksanaan langkah pembetulan ralat itu sendiri.\n"
"Ini kembali kepada idea bahawa apa sahaja yang melibatkan maklumat kuantum terdedah kepada ralat — termasuk litar yang sendirinya bertujuan untuk membetulkan ralat.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Consider, for instance, the type of circuit described in \"The stabilizer formalism\" lesson for measuring stabilizer generators non-destructively using phase estimation.\n"
"These circuits are clearly not fault-tolerant because they can cause errors to propagate within the code block on which they operate.\n"
"This might seem rather problematic, but there are multiple known ways to perform error correction fault-tolerantly in a way that does not cause errors to propagate within the code blocks being corrected.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pertimbangkan, sebagai contoh, jenis litar yang diterangkan dalam pelajaran \"Formalisme penstabil\" untuk mengukur penjana penstabil secara tidak merosakkan menggunakan anggaran fasa.\n"
"Litar-litar ini jelas tidak toleran ralat kerana ia boleh menyebabkan ralat merambat dalam blok kod yang beroperasi ke atasnya.\n"
"Ini mungkin kelihatan cukup bermasalah, tetapi terdapat pelbagai cara yang diketahui untuk melakukan pembetulan ralat secara toleran ralat dengan cara yang tidak menyebabkan ralat merambat dalam blok kod yang sedang dibetulkan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"One method is known as *Shor error correction,* because it was first discovered by Peter Shor.\n"
"The idea is to perform syndrome measurements using a so-called *cat state,* which is an $n$-qubit state of the form\n"
msgstr ""
"Satu kaedah dikenali sebagai *pembetulan ralat Shor,* kerana ia pertama kali ditemui oleh Peter Shor.\n"
"Ideanya ialah melakukan pengukuran sindrom menggunakan apa yang dipanggil *keadaan kucing,* iaitu keadaan $n$-qubit dalam bentuk\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0^n \\rangle + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 1^n \\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0^n \\rangle + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 1^n \\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where $0^n$ and $1^n$ refer to the all-zero and all-one strings of length $n.$\n"
"For instance, this is a $\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle$ state when $n=2$ and a GHZ state when $n=3,$ but in general, Shor error correction requires a state like this for $n$ being the weight of the stabilizer generator being measured.\n"
msgstr ""
"di mana $0^n$ dan $1^n$ merujuk kepada rentetan semua-sifar dan semua-satu dengan panjang $n.$\n"
"Sebagai contoh, ini adalah keadaan $\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle$ apabila $n=2$ dan keadaan GHZ apabila $n=3,$ tetapi secara amnya, pembetulan ralat Shor memerlukan keadaan seperti ini untuk $n$ yang merupakan berat penjana penstabil yang sedang diukur.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As an example, the circuit shown here measures a stabilizer generator of the"
" form $P_2\\otimes P_1 \\otimes P_0.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Sebagai contoh, litar yang ditunjukkan di sini mengukur penjana penstabil "
"dalam bentuk $P_2\\otimes P_1 \\otimes P_0.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![A Shor error detection circuit](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-"
"quantum-error-correction/fault-tolerant-quantum-computing/Shor-error-"
"detection.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![A Shor error detection circuit](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-"
"quantum-error-correction/fault-tolerant-quantum-computing/Shor-error-"
"detection.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This necessitates the construction of the cat state itself, and to make it "
"work reliably in the presence of errors and potentially faulty gates, the "
"method actually requires repeatedly running circuits like this to make "
"inferences about where different errors may have occurred during the "
"process.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ini memerlukan pembinaan keadaan kucing itu sendiri, dan untuk menjadikannya"
" berfungsi dengan boleh dipercayai dengan kehadiran ralat dan get yang "
"berpotensi rosak, kaedah ini sebenarnya memerlukan litar seperti ini "
"dijalankan berulang kali untuk membuat inferens tentang di mana ralat yang "
"berbeza mungkin telah berlaku semasa proses berlangsung.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"An alternative method is known as *Steane error correction.*\n"
"This method works differently, and it only works for CSS codes.\n"
"The idea is that we don't actually perform the syndrome measurements on the encoded quantum states in the circuit we're trying to run, but instead we *intentionally* propagate errors to a workspace system, and then measure that system and *classically* detect errors.\n"
"The following circuit diagrams illustrate how this can be done for detecting $X$ and $Z$ errors, respectively.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kaedah alternatif dikenali sebagai *pembetulan ralat Steane.*\n"
"Kaedah ini berfungsi secara berbeza, dan ia hanya berfungsi untuk kod CSS.\n"
"Ideanya ialah kita sebenarnya tidak melakukan pengukuran sindrom pada keadaan kuantum yang dikodkan dalam litar yang cuba kita jalankan, tetapi sebaliknya kita *sengaja* merambatkan ralat ke sistem ruang kerja, dan kemudian mengukur sistem itu dan mengesan ralat secara *klasik*.\n"
"Gambar rajah litar berikut menggambarkan bagaimana ini boleh dilakukan untuk mengesan ralat $X$ dan $Z$, masing-masing.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![A Steane error detection circuit](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-"
"quantum-error-correction/fault-tolerant-quantum-computing/Steane-error-"
"detection.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![A Steane error detection circuit](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-"
"quantum-error-correction/fault-tolerant-quantum-computing/Steane-error-"
"detection.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A related method known as *Knill error correction* extends this method to "
"arbitrary stabilizer codes using teleportation.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kaedah berkaitan yang dikenali sebagai *pembetulan ralat Knill* melanjutkan "
"kaedah ini ke kod penstabil sewenang-wenangnya menggunakan teleportasi.\n"
